**How to implement.** The Data locations screen: its rows, its message and its view, as a pure Elmish update over injected seams (001 §G 'a Launcher Data locations panel shows them, each with Open folder'; the S5.3 brief: it lists every DataLocations entry with its path and Open folder, which opens Explorer through a seam tests substitute; .spec-md §4 'UI'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type DataLocationKind with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Library database`, `Library backups`, `Preferences`, `Kit folders (suggested parent)`, `Exports`, `Catalogue exports` and `Shipped catalogue`) and `member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`LibraryDatabase`, `LibraryBackups`, `Preferences`, `Kits`, `Exports`, `Catalogues` and `ShippedCatalogue`); and `ConstructorUiId.dataLocationRow`, `dataLocationPathText` and `dataLocationOpenFolderButton`, each over a `DataLocationKind` (`DataLocationRow_<key>`, `DataLocationPath_<key>`, `DataLocationOpenFolder_<key>`). `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the kit-bar group (step 188), `// --- The Data locations window (DataLocationsView, DataLocationsWindow). ---`, holding `dataLocationsStatusText` (`"DataLocationsStatusText"`) with a one-line doc. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView`, compiled directly after `KitWindowView.fs` (step 188): one `<Compile>` line and no comment; its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3. It follows `KitStartView.fs` (step 176). (a) `DataLocationRow = { kind : DataLocationKind; path : ControlCaption; folderOpt : FolderName option }`: what a listed location shows and the folder Open folder opens, `None` when there is none. (b) `type DataLocations with member this.rows : DataLocationRow list` answers one row per `DataLocationKind.all` (step 192), in that order: the library database row shows `LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf this.libraryConnection`'s full path and opens its folder (`Path.GetDirectoryName`), and for an in-memory library shows `In memory (<the connection string>)` with no folder; every other row shows its folder's text and opens that folder. It reads no disk: a folder that does not exist yet is listed, and Open folder tells it. (c) `[<ReferenceEquality>] DataLocationsContext = { locations : DataLocations; explorer : ExplorerProxy }` (step 182). (d) `DataLocationsModel = { context : DataLocationsContext; rows : DataLocationRow list; status : ControlCaption option }`. (e) `DataLocationsMsg` = `OpenDataLocationFolder of DataLocationKind`. (f) `initDataLocations (context : DataLocationsContext) : DataLocationsModel` answers `context.locations.rows` and no status. (g) `updateDataLocations (msg : DataLocationsMsg) (m : DataLocationsModel) : DataLocationsModel`: for the row of the kind, a folder is handed to `m.context.explorer.showFolder`, `Ok ()` clearing `status` and `Error e` setting it to `The folder could not be opened — <e.describe>`; a row without a folder answers the model unchanged. (h) `dataLocationsView (m : DataLocationsModel) (dispatch : DataLocationsMsg -> unit) : IView`, a pure projection: a `ScrollViewer` over a `MinWidthPanel` of minimum width 480, both scroll bars `Auto`, as `kitStartView` scrolls (step 178), over a vertical `StackPanel` holding the status, when `Some`, as a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `dataLocationsStatusText` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`, then one `DockPanel` per row carrying `dataLocationRow kind`, whose right side holds, for a row with a folder, the `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` `Open folder` (`dataLocationOpenFolderButton kind`, sending `OpenDataLocationFolder kind`) and whose fill is a vertical `StackPanel` of the semi-bold `kind.caption` and a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `dataLocationPathText kind` with the path. No edit field, copy button or cache is added: the locations are edited in `appsettings.json` (001 §G). (3) Tests. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataLocationsTests.fs`, `module DataLocationsTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over `DataLocations` built in the fact with folders under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "DataLocationsTests")` and a recording explorer: `the rows list every location in order, the library by its file`: over a file library `Data Source=<folder>/library.db` the seven rows follow `DataLocationKind.all`, the library row shows the file's full path and opens `<folder>`, and the kits row shows and opens the kits folder. `an in-memory library is listed without a folder`: over `Data Source=:memory:` the library row reads `In memory (Data Source=:memory:)` and has no folder. `Open folder hands the row's folder to the explorer`: `OpenDataLocationFolder KitsLocation` records the kits folder and leaves no status, and over the in-memory library `OpenDataLocationFolder LibraryDatabaseLocation` records nothing. `a folder the explorer cannot open is told`: over an explorer answering `Error (MissingFolderErr "gone")`, the status contains `gone`. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs`, `module DataLocationsWindowTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounts the view as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts one (`:107`), headless at 800 × 600, over `TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName "DataLocationsWindowTests")` (step 83) and a recording explorer. Without a trait: `the Data locations UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: `dataLocationsStatusText` and the three ids of `KitsLocation`. `every location is listed with its path, and Open folder only where there is a folder`: each kind's `dataLocationRow` and `dataLocationPathText` exist, the kits row's path is the test kits folder's text, and the in-memory library's row has no `dataLocationOpenFolderButton` while every other row has one. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing Open folder hands that location's folder to the explorer`: pressing the exports row's button records the exports folder.

**Acceptance.** After the Data locations view lands, `DataLocations.rows` MUST list the seven locations with their paths and folders, the in-memory library without one, and `updateDataLocations` MUST hand a row's folder to the context's explorer and tell a refusal; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the rows list every location in order, the library by its file`, `an in-memory library is listed without a folder`, `Open folder hands the row's folder to the explorer` and `a folder the explorer cannot open is told`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Open folder hands that location's folder to the explorer`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Data locations UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `every location is listed with its path, and Open folder only where there is a folder`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
